id: monica-openapi-edition-contracts
title: Publish edition-aware OpenAPI and compatibility contracts
description: "Generate validated OpenAPI 3.2.0 and 3.1.2 documents plus deterministic stable-to-next compatibility diffs from authoritative Monica route references, with executable CLI links, source provenance, CI gates, agent-safe output, and current toolchain support."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[11]: agent-ux,api-contracts,api-research,ci,compatibility,documentation,openapi,provenance,read-only-safety,sdk-generation,typescript
created_at: "2026-07-27T21:16:50.448Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T22:04:53.675Z"
deadline: "2026-08-03T21:16:50.448Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T22:04:52.946Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "OpenAPI export defaults to the latest published OAS 3.2.0 and supports OAS 3.1.2 compatibility output; both cover all 172 stable endpoints and all 9 next endpoints with deterministic unique operation IDs, normalized path parameters, authentication, source provenance, CLI mapping, request/response metadata, and JSON/YAML interoperability; Edition diff reports added, removed, and changed operations deterministically and offers a failing CI gate for incompatible changes; Contract validation rejects duplicate operations, undeclared path parameters, invalid methods, missing mappings, stale provenance, and schema-invalid output without network or CRM writes; Default TOON plus JSON, YAML, Markdown, and table output remain schema-valid; help and docs describe exact commands and agent workflows; Exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage, 100 percent docstrings, under-300 code LOC, duplication/security/privacy/package/PM/release gates, and actual read-only monica acceptance all pass"
definition_of_ready: "All 62 PM items and verified histories reviewed; duplicate scan clear; official stable and main heads, routes, controllers, resources, and current package versions refreshed; clean branch based on v2026.7.26"
goal: monica-platform
objective: portable-machine-api-contracts
value: "Enable standard SDK generation, CI compatibility gates, and zero-guesswork agent integration across Monica API editions."
impact: Consumers can adopt Monica APIs through a validated ecosystem-standard contract while detecting upstream edition drift before runtime.
outcome: Every authoritative Monica API operation is portable as OpenAPI and mechanically comparable across editions.
why_now: "Endpoint parity is complete, so the highest-leverage remaining API enhancement is a portable validated contract instead of another bespoke wrapper."
parent: monica-platform
reviewer: github-bots
risk: high
confidence: 95
sprint: 2026-07-openapi-contracts
release: next
reporter: codex-root
severity: high
environment: Monica stable 4.x v4.1.2 and current main; monica-cli 2026.7.26; Bun 1.3.11; Node 22+; private instance read-only
repro_steps: "Run monica api-research --help and monica schemas list: no OpenAPI export, edition diff, or cross-contract validation command exists despite complete bundled route references."
resolution: "Implemented deterministic edition-aware OpenAPI export, structural and provenance validation, breaking-change diffing, output schemas, release gates, enriched authoritative metadata, and read-only acceptance coverage."
expected_result: "Agents, CI, and SDK generators can consume and validate a provenance-rich OpenAPI 3.2.0 or 3.1.2 document for either Monica edition and detect compatibility changes deterministically."
actual_result: "The CLI exports all 172 stable and 9 current operations as OAS 3.2.0 or 3.1.2, validates and diffs them deterministically, exposes registered schemas and complete help, and passes every production/read-only gate."
affected_version: 2026.7.26
fixed_version: next
component: api-contracts
regression: false
customer_impact: Automated consumers must duplicate contract interpretation and cannot reliably detect breaking edition changes before deployment.
