comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:50.448Z",codex-root,Duplicate research covered all 62 PM items and exact OpenAPI specification edition-diff SDK-generation queries; no canonical item exists.
  "2026-07-27T21:16:53.880Z",codex-root,"The duplicate review additionally verified all 382 history entries and a 985-pair similarity scan with zero clusters at threshold 0.72. Existing parity, provenance, TOON, and agent-contract items are closed predecessors rather than duplicates."
  "2026-07-27T21:18:23.244Z",codex-root,OpenAPI Initiative sources verified that 3.2.0 is the latest published specification and 3.1.2 is the latest 3.1 patch. Default export will be 3.2.0; --oas-version 3.1.2 provides compatibility for generators that have not adopted 3.2.
  "2026-07-27T21:37:02.899Z",codex-root,Implementation covers 172 stable operations and 9 current-main operations. Offline strict validation currently reports zero errors and zero warnings for both editions; JSON/YAML exports parse and source files remain private-data-free.
  "2026-07-27T22:04:52.237Z",codex-root,"Final local evidence: PM ran all 6 linked gates successfully. Coverage is 3648/3648 statements, 2271/2271 branches, 1133/1133 functions, and 3352/3352 lines; 877 tests and 288 help nodes passed; Redocly reports zero findings for stable OAS 3.2 and next OAS 3.1; live public source heads are current; read-only acceptance completed 117 checks with 61 pass, 56 expected server-unavailable classifications, and zero unexpected failures; every mutation probe was blocked before dispatch."
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:50.448Z",codex-root,Official stable and current route/controller/resource research is public-only; private settings and payloads remain outside Git and PM.
  "2026-07-27T21:16:54.876Z",codex-root,"Official research refreshed 2026-07-27: stable release v4.1.2 and branch 4.x remain at 32028ce; current main remains at e08e917 with three user and six vault routes. Current controllers use Scribe attributes for query, body, and response contracts."
  "2026-07-27T21:18:24.068Z",codex-root,"OAS documents are valid JSON objects representable as JSON or YAML. TOON, Markdown, and table remain CLI presentation formats; JSON/YAML are the standards-interchange modes documented for OpenAPI tooling."
  "2026-07-27T21:37:03.865Z",codex-root,"Dependency refresh uses current @toon-format/toon 4.1.0, @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog 2026.7.27, ESLint 10.8.0, eslint-plugin-jsdoc 63.3.1, globals 17.8.0, and jscpd 5.0.14. TypeScript 7 remains isolated in the canonical compatibility spike because this repository still intentionally targets the proven TypeScript 6 and Node 22 baseline."
  "2026-07-27T21:52:27.882Z",codex-root,Independent validation is now a mandatory release gate using pinned @redocly/cli 2.41.0. Explicit AGPL-3.0-only metadata and 401 error responses reduced both OAS 3.2 stable and OAS 3.1.2 next lint results to zero findings.
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T21:16:50.448Z",codex-root,Endpoint parity still needs portable operation identity security request response validation and compatibility semantics.
  "2026-07-27T21:16:55.960Z",codex-root,A complete portable contract must preserve edition boundaries rather than merging stable OAuth and current Sanctum operations into a misleading single compatibility target.
  "2026-07-27T21:37:05.002Z",codex-root,"A useful Monica contract validator must enforce semantic invariants beyond JSON shape: unique method-path keys and operation IDs, declared path parameters, bearer security, response metadata, edition provenance, and truthful CLI mappings."
