close_reason: "Delivered validated edition-aware OpenAPI export, compatibility diffing, strict internal and independent contract gates, enriched authoritative references, full agent documentation, current tooling, and safe real-instance acceptance with every criterion satisfied."
body: "## Context\nOfficial research confirms stable 4.x and current main route inventories are unchanged and fully mapped, but the CLI previously exposed no industry-standard API document or deterministic edition compatibility report.\n\n## Delivery\n- Enrich authoritative edition metadata from official routes, controllers, Scribe attributes, and resources.\n- Export deterministic OpenAPI 3.2.0 by default with 3.1.2 compatibility, bearer security, parameters, request bodies, responses, unique operation IDs, CLI extensions, and source provenance.\n- Add edition diff and contract validation commands with explicit CI failure modes.\n- Register output schemas and update help, docs, agent catalogs, read-only acceptance, and package/release tooling.\n\n## Safety\nContract generation and validation are offline/read-only. Live acceptance remains GET-only with readOnlyMode enabled; credentials, identifiers, response bodies, and private topology stay outside Git, PM, logs, and GitHub."
